  "id": "Compound::DB00116 - Gene::10797",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Tetrahydrofolic Acid (THFA) and Mthfd2, as THFA binds to Mthfd1, which is involved in multiple enzymatic activities related to folate metabolism. These activities include the conversion of methylenetetrahydrofolate to tetrahydrofolate and the hydrolysis of methenyltetrahydrofolate, both of which are critical in maintaining folate homeostasis. The fact that THFA interacts with Mthfd1 and that Mthfd2 participates in these activities indicates that THFA may influence Mthfd2 through a shared pathway involving Mthfd1. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust and reliable relationship, supported by the direct interaction between THFA and Mthfd1, and the involvement of Mthfd2 in the enzymatic processes catalyzed by Mthfd1. This integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that THFA may modulate Mthfd2 through a mechanism involving Mthfd1, potentially affecting folate metabolism and downstream biological processes.",
